Planning organized the work into an eight-week schedule. The first week was used to finalize the idea and gather requirements, the second week for design and database planning, weeks three and four for backend and face recognition development, the fifth week for the frontend and dashboard, the sixth week for integration and testing, the seventh week for bug fixing and documentation, and the final week for review, presentation preparation, and the demonstration. Roles were distributed among a project lead, backend developer, frontend developer, tester, and documentation lead. A risk assessment identified poor lighting as a threat to accuracy, which would be handled through image preprocessing and a manual override, and it identified data privacy as a serious concern, which would be addressed through encryption and user consent. Possible team member unavailability and deadline slips were to be managed through cross-training, weekly reviews, and buffer time.
